course: dictionary
lesson: 5416
title: Lactase and milk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lactase is an enzyme, which is a natural chemical your body makes to help with a job. Its job is to break down lactose, the sugar found in milk, so that your body can digest it.
explain: «Many adults lose most of lactase, the body chemical that breaks down milk sugar, so milk gives them gas and a sore tummy.» The sentence tells you two things: lactase breaks down milk sugar, and without enough of it, milk can upset the tummy.
explain: Think of lactase as a helper that cuts milk sugar into smaller pieces. If there is not enough helper, the sugar is not broken down properly, and the tummy may ache.
fact: Lactase is an enzyme, a natural chemical made in the body.
fact: Lactase breaks down lactose, the sugar found in milk.
fact: When a person does not have enough lactase, milk can cause gas and a sore tummy. This is called lactose intolerance.
fact: Lactase drops or pills can help people who do not have enough lactase.
fact: In the example, about two thirds of the world's adults lose most of their lactase, but this happens much less in northern Europe.
exercise: What does lactase do? | Makes milk colder | *Breaks down lactose, the sugar in milk | Turns milk into cheese
exercise: Why can lactase drops or pills help some people? | They stop the body needing food | They make milk sweeter | *They help the body break down milk sugar | They make the tummy grow
exercise: Lactase is called an enzyme. What is an enzyme? | A type of milk | A kind of sugar that is always bad for you | A fizzy drink | *A natural chemical in the body that helps a job happen
test: When a person does not have enough lactase and milk gives them a sore tummy, what is this problem called? | Lactase drops | Enzyme cheese | *Lactose intolerance
test: Which statement about lactase is true? | *It is a chemical that breaks down milk sugar | It is a sugar found in fizzy drinks | It is a type of milk
exam: Why does milk make some adults' tummies sore, according to the example? | The sugar makes them sleepy | *They do not have enough lactase to break down milk sugar | Their bodies have too much milk | Milk is always sour
